{"skill":{"slug":"git-essentials","displayName":"Git Essentials"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769692045864,"changelog":"Initial release of git-essentials.\n\n- Provides essential Git commands for setup, version control, branching, remote operations, stashing, rebasing, tagging, submodules, and cleaning.\n- Includes common workflows for feature branches, hotfixes, and syncing forks.\n- Offers helpful aliases, practical tips, and solutions to common issues.\n- Links to official Git documentation and resources for further learning.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7074,"sha256":"91afbc572326eb63a249a96f7880a21d1a0288f09b7d833cc616a184ce5ca71f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1830,"sha256":"7708e065efa82d8c2ab9ba5db054a119ca407b08d13cb039e2cd4759c942cb69","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789023419331,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"70ce7450ac7b6b4b81e1cae9f40986d3f6422ec252317bbf1362f1a48435f0cb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/70ce7450ac7b6b4b81e1cae9f40986d3f6422ec252317bbf1362f1a48435f0cb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: git-essentials\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle 'git-essentials' is a comprehensive guide to Git commands and workflows. All content in SKILL.md consists of standard Git command examples and explanations, without any evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, or prompt injection attempts against the AI agent. The requested 'git' binary in the metadata is appropriate for the skill's stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160294235},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":43,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789023419331},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a Git command reference with some risky Git examples, but no hidden execution or unrelated behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill may lead an agent to use Git commands that modify repositories and optionally global Git configuration, which is normal for a Git reference but can affect local work if used carelessly.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install script, executable component, dependency fetch, remote payload execution, or tool wrapping was present; metadata only declares a git binary requirement.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"It includes destructive or history-rewriting Git examples such as reset --hard, clean -fdx, branch -D, stash clear, and force-with-lease; these are relevant to Git usage but should be treated as commands to run only with explicit user intent.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The only persistent changes described are standard Git global configuration and optional ~/.gitconfig aliases; there are no services, hooks, background workers, credential handling, or cross-session agent modifications.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a Markdown-only Git essentials guide covering setup, branching, remotes, history, undo, stashing, rebasing, tags, submodules, cleaning, workflows, aliases, and documentation links, which matches its stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want Git command help. Before allowing an agent to run commands from the undo, clean, delete, or force-push sections, review git status and confirm you are comfortable losing local changes or rewriting remote history.","findings":"[TM1] expected: The flagged commands are ordinary Git operations documented as examples, not evidence of parameter abuse or hidden tool misuse in this Markdown-only skill.\n[SQP-2] expected: The concern is partly valid as user guidance: destructive Git commands are present and warnings are brief, but the commands are plainly labeled for discarding, deleting, or force-pushing and are purpose-aligned.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789023419331}}}}}